{"id": "EUVD-2026-103733", "enisaUuid": "9e6726e9-e95d-3da8-be60-e7daa23ecded", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: ipconfig: bound DHCP option construction\n\nic_dhcp_init_options() appends the hostname (option 12), vendor-class\n(option 60) and client-ID (option 61) options into the fixed 312-byte\nbootp_pkt.exten[] buffer.  Only the client-ID branch checked the\nremaining space; the hostname and vendor-class writes were unbounded.\n\nA 64-byte hostname together with the maximum 252-byte dhcpclass=\nidentifier needs 18 + (2 + 64) + (2 + 252) = 338 of the 312 available\nbytes even before the terminating END marker, so the vendor-class memcpy\nruns past the end of exten[].  With CONFIG_FORTIFY_SOURCE this is\nreported as a field-spanning write and, when the kernel is booted with\npanic_on_warn=1, aborts boot with a panic.\n\nRoute the optional options through a common helper that makes sure the\noption, its 2-byte header and the END marker all fit and drops an option\nthat would not.  Configurations with short options keep sending exactly\nthe same bytes as before.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:16:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/38a6a118260ebfc82d0c653194d616bdfbd236ac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/abcba6f080c63e403037ecdffde43170d242376a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/24e79508b237dd2a69bc6fb6ac5cf7f126178307", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cbaad2922bd5d4d303055ae9afecc8999e6b40c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e47a1958e12abc3a17b5231a4f21c8f1bf662e08"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98493", "GHSA-x4fq-3fw2-872x"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "500b72d6-4435-3df4-980d-c00b5bcd53cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "130c0f47fdf9c533deb1136cad5136f6cb7020f0 <abcba6f080c63e403037ecdffde43170d242376a"}, {"id": "57d0204c-25d9-3b28-83b7-f303355487b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "5aa4d38f-59d7-3d17-abef-c4ba72fba6d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "8257195b-cf19-3835-9a61-7a067d455271", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "130c0f47fdf9c533deb1136cad5136f6cb7020f0 <38a6a118260ebfc82d0c653194d616bdfbd236ac"}, {"id": "97918c74-b4ea-371c-a679-df4c7df92724", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "130c0f47fdf9c533deb1136cad5136f6cb7020f0 <cbaad2922bd5d4d303055ae9afecc8999e6b40c9"}, {"id": "a374b57a-3068-3fed-abf6-64fc5837987b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "130c0f47fdf9c533deb1136cad5136f6cb7020f0 <e47a1958e12abc3a17b5231a4f21c8f1bf662e08"}, {"id": "a53707fc-a6de-3247-8bad-7c6d429cac95", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "aed34416-467d-35c7-9582-1c28cff60905", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.36"}, {"id": "b270577c-3272-3284-9aa6-5d6873033e11", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "d7a1658b-da79-38c5-b7da-531f4b71fee1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "e47143ad-9145-3efa-9c42-f77b6c441594", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e5e31992-c938-390f-9c7d-4abf54c15129", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "130c0f47fdf9c533deb1136cad5136f6cb7020f0 <24e79508b237dd2a69bc6fb6ac5cf7f126178307"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1d02d653-a909-3d2f-af2b-257e9fb156e9", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}